  ],
  "preconditions": [
    "Synthetic native project, exact parsed candidates/input/mapping bytes, complete supplied TargetModel, explicit actor/request/time/policy and separate trusted host publication authority. Existing attachment bytes are already part of the bound base."
  ],
  "steps": [
    "Publish a fresh or explicitly reassessed saved loss-free import plan through the ordinary native writer; compare actual files, revisions, identity history, whole-target root and durable transaction receipt.",
    "Repeat the same request, including a changed plan envelope with identical operations: verify original receipt/audit and no new lock or publication. Conflicting operations under that request fail without modifying its receipt.",
    "Check no-op authorization, invalid/lossy/conflicting targets, forged or stale saved inputs, changed live base/resource/attachment bytes, missing gates, actor/request refusals and interrupted staging. Verify preserved bytes and real native recovery state.",
    "Exercise an existing bound attachment with an imported source reference and another artifact in one complete target; run real native execution and replay in isolated Core and PYZ runtimes.",
    "Report expected import failures without manufacturing completion, loss consent or rollback. Interrupt both real artifact replacements before and after the syscall; block ordinary reads/retries, explicitly recover to the exact basis or complete target, and verify original receipts and unrelated bytes."
  ],
  "oracle": {
    "kind": "behavior",
    "requirement_contract": "`specroad import apply <FORMAT> <INPUT> [--plan <FILE>]` MUSS einen zuvor ausgegebenen oder im selben Aufruf erzeugten gültigen Importplan über den gemeinsamen Change-Plan-, Transaktions- und Recovery-Vertrag anwenden und ein übergebenes Planfile exakt an Eingabe und aktuelle Basis binden.",
    "scope": "14.e.W adds apply_import_plan for explicit already-parsed artifact candidates. Fresh and saved plans undergo the same mapping/conflict/loss/complete-target assessment before the shared native writer performs live checks, locking, authorization, journaling, publication, receipt and cleanup. A saved envelope never supplies authority. Native exceptions and recovery states propagate without automatic retry or rollback. submitted_import_plan is passive and belongs to this call; execution separately reports actual native publication or historical replay. Replays retain original actor/time/plan/created IDs/receipt and do not claim a newly verified current target. No-ops require authorization but create no receipt or revision. Existing attachment bytes remain bound and unchanged. CLI/source parsing, incoming attachment creation, relation/registry imports, loss-acceptance workflow remain open; this is not full requirement or release completion. 14.e.R adds execute_import_plan, preserving the raising API. Failure reports retain only freshly assessed submitted plans, never untrusted saved observations. Expected model/security/I/O failures retain native exits and proven write states; missing writer evidence is unknown with recovery required. No automatic retry, rollback or approval. Multiple artifact publication interrupted at each replacement boundary stays quarantined from ordinary reads; explicit native recovery restores the exact basis or completes the entire target with durable original receipts. Full targets are never rolled back. Late staging/receipt/cleanup failures retain actual operational state. Unexpected programming errors propagate. This covers the existing explicit artifact-candidate profile, not future source-format parsing or loss-acceptance workflows. 14.e.C separates passive execution/failure report projection into one private module and keeps both public entry points on the same format-independent native publication route with explicit keyword-bound writer arguments. Public signatures, output fields, native exit codes, write-state conservatism, authorization, input ownership, replay and recovery effects remain unchanged. Existing W/R behavior tests and their identities/oracles are retained; no new product capability or completed requirement is claimed."
  },
